       The routine cchhggaatt changes the attributes of a given number  of  charac‐
       ters  starting  at  the current cursor location of ssttddssccrr.  It does not
       update the cursor and does not perform wrapping.  A character count  of
       -1  or  greater  than  the  remaining  window width means to change at‐
       tributes all the way to the end of the current line.  The wwcchhggaatt  func‐
       tion  generalizes this to any window; the mmvvwwcchhggaatt function does a cur‐
       sor move before acting.

       In these functions, the color _p_a_i_r argument is a color pair  index  (as
       in the first argument of iinniitt__ppaaiirr, see ccuurrss__ccoolloorr(3X)).

