       All routines return the integer OOKK on success, or EERRRR on failure.

       X/Open Curses does not specify any error conditions.

       This implementation

       •   returns an error if the window pointer is null.

       •   returns an error if the color pair parameter for wwccoolloorr__sseett is out‐
           side the range 0..COLOR_PAIRS-1.

       •   does not return an error if either of the parameters  of  wwaattttrr__ggeett
           used for retrieving attribute or color pair values is NNUULLLL.

       Functions  prefixed with “mv” first perform cursor movement and fail if
       the position (_y, _x) is outside the window boundaries.

